<h1>05 - ASP.NET Core Identity</h1>

<p>
    Same app as 01, but our hand-written <code>UserService</code> and <code>SignInAsync</code> code
    is replaced by ASP.NET Core Identity: users and their claims live in a database
    (<code>AppDbContext</code>), and <code>SignInManager.PasswordSignInAsync</code> does the login.
</p>

<ul>
    <li><b>Secret</b> shows the claims Identity puts into the cookie (more than we added ourselves in 01).</li>
    <li><b>Admin</b> requires the <code>IsAdmin</code> claim, stored in the database for the admin user.</li>
</ul>
